  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct Humanitarian Assistance to Vulnerable Populations Affected by Forced Displacement in Niger - Phase VIII</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to provide humanitarian assistance to populations in vulnerable situations that are affected by forced displacement in Niger, while promoting community mobilization and empowerment. Specifically, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing shelter and non-food item assistance to refugees and internally displaced persons, as well as supporting capacity building efforts for humanitarian actors, in regions heavy conflict including Diffa, Tahoua, Tillaberi, Agadez and Maradi. This project contributes towards the Protection Cluster Strategy for 2024 in Niger and prioritizes the provision of assistance to households with specific needs, such as older persons, people with disabilities and pregnant women, in line with institutional and global protection mainstreaming policies.</narrative>
  </description>
